    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0731" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2214</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Messrs. J. P. Morgan &amp; Company</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: The Department has been holding your
                    letter of August 23, 1921, while endeavoring to secure more exact information as
                    to the indebtedness of the Chinese Eastern Railway Company.</p>
                <pb facs="0732" n="608" xml:id="pg608"/>
                <p>Mr. John F. Stevens. President of the Allied Technical Board of the railway, is
                    now <hi rendition="#italic">en route</hi> to the United States with statistics
                    and other information regarding the financial condition of the Chinese Eastern.
                    After his arrival the Department will again consider with the American Group the
                    possibility of a consortium loan.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. M.
                            Dearing</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                        Secretary</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
